<title>USA: U.S. rice weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. rice weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA rice export sales highlights in latest reporting week:</p>
<p>Sales of 49,200 MT were more than ten times the prior week and three and one-tenth times the 4-week average.</p>
<p>The primary buyer was Costa Rica (26,500 MT--all rough), with smaller sales to the Netherlands (5,300 MT), Saudi Arabia (4,600 MT), Haiti (3,200 MT), the Netherlands Antilles (2,500 MT), Nicaragua (2,000 MT), Mexico (1,300 MT--all rough), and Honduras (1,300 MT).</p>
<p>In addition, rough rice sales of 400 MT were reported for Guatemala.</p>
<p>Exports of 54,500 MT were three times the previous week and 9 percent above the 4-week average.  The major destinations were the Netherlands (16,600 MT), Guatemala (8,700 MT), Saudi Arabia (7,800 MT), South Africa (4,500 MT), and Haiti (3,200 MT).</p>
</text>
